    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d547">

                <pb facs="0563" n="557" sameAs="frus:frus1942v02/pg557"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">125.226/2: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Leopoldville (Motion) to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Leopoldville</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-04-04T12:00:00+01:00">April 4,
                            1942—noon.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 5:42 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>73. Referred to in the Department’s telegram number 39, April 2, 9 a.m. [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">p.m.</hi>]. High Commissioner agreeable to establishment
                    of Consulate at Brazzaville and delighted to accept Laurence W. Taylor as
                        Consul.<anchor n="90" xml:id="d547-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mallon</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d547-f1" n="90" xml:id="d547-f1-content">
                <p>Public announcement was made on April 4, 1942; see Department of State <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi>, April 4, 1942, p. 273.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
